        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "582cb72b-5387-5858-a620-ada4a7653342",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: That Darn Cat!, Perri, The Ugly Dachshund, The Love Bug, The Million Dollar Duck, Beethoven\n- People: Dean Jones, Suzanne Pleshette, Felix Salten\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Topics: Disney live-action films, film roles\n\nFacts:\n- \"Perri\" is a 1957 film from Walt Disney Productions based on Felix Salten's 1938 work \"Perri: The Youth of a Squirrel.\"\n- Dean Jones played a role in \"That Darn Cat!\" in 1965.\n- \"The Ugly Dachshund\" is a 1966 Walt Disney Productions feature film starring Dean Jones and Suzanne Pleshette about a Great Dane who believes he is a dachshund.\n- Dean Jones played Jim Douglas in \"The Love Bug\" in 1968.\n- Dean Jones played Albert Dooley in \"The Million Dollar Duck\" in 1971 and received a Golden Globe nomination for that role.\n- Dean Jones played Dr. Herman Varnick in \"Beethoven\" in 1992.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
